# Jaguar XJ Series 3 four-door saloon, 1979-1992.
#
# The Pininfarina restyle of the XJ: a revised roofline with narrower door
# frames and more glass area, body-colour rather than chrome-framed roof
# pillars, a more pronounced Hofmeister kink, a larger grille and revised
# bumpers. The longest-running XJ and the largest class-3/4 Jaguar parc of the
# 1980s.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_XJ_(Series_3)
#
# Dimensions 4.959 x 1.770 x 1.377 m, wheelbase 2.865 m.
#
# Shape reference: a near-side view about 15-20 degrees behind square, the most
# side-on Series 3 found; the boot lid is open and the bumpers are North
# American. The flank and tail are reconciled against the front three-quarter
# and the grille detail within the published dimensions. Recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d), Jaguar BLVC paint-code tables rather than a UK brochure.
# Regent Grey 315, Rhodium Silver MDE, Sebring Red CDJ and Cobalt Blue 286 are
# period names. Weights 15, 14, 13, 13, total 55, reflecting the model's UK
# volume, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 210 km/h. Comfort 130/525, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 130. Classes 3,4.
# Dates 1979-1992 production, road tail staggered 2007-2010.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-xj-series3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-xj-series3.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-xj-series3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: no true side elevation exists; the side image is about
# 15-20 degrees behind square, with the boot lid open and North American bumpers.
# The flank was reconciled against the front three-quarter and grille detail
# within the published dimensions; the open boot and bumper equipment are not
# copied as body shape. Lamp and grille detail is simplified.


